# Binary files must never be line-ending converted.
#
# ⚠️ Git warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" when committing docs/one_pager.pdf,
# which is git offering to corrupt a binary. Nothing was damaged on the way in — the
# stored blob is byte-identical — but the conversion also runs on CHECKOUT, so a
# reviewer cloning on a machine with core.autocrlf=true could have ended up with a
# broken PDF and no idea why. The database is the worse case: a corrupted SQLite file
# fails at import time with something unhelpful.
#
# Marking them binary settles it in both directions, for every clone.
*.pdf   binary
*.docx  binary
*.db    binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary

# Text files: normalise to LF in the repository, whatever the author's platform does
# locally. This repo was written on Windows and will be read on macOS and Linux.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.html  text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
